The legal texts are the Constitution of Oregon and chapters 60, 93, 163 and 164 of the Oregon Revised Statutes, as published by the Oregon Legislature (Legislative Counsel) (oregonlegislature.gov). Statutes and constitutions are
not copyrightable subject matter (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, 2020); only the law text is taken, never annotations, notes
or editorial material. The bytes were read from Internet Archive captures of the official pages; the Legislature is the publisher. Its robots.txt (archived 2025) disallows nothing.
Source: the Oregon Legislature (Legislative Counsel), oregonlegislature.gov.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This
repository is not legal advice and not an official publication.
